  "tagline": "Spark's SQL and DataFrame engine for large-scale batch, streaming and lakehouse processing.",
  "description": "Spark SQL is the relational layer of Apache Spark: the Catalyst optimizer and Tungsten execution engine behind SQL, DataFrames and Structured Streaming. It reads and writes Parquet, ORC, Delta Lake, Iceberg and Hudi on object storage and is the workhorse of most lakehouse ETL. Spark 4.x brought ANSI SQL mode by default, the VARIANT type, SQL scripting, Spark Connect thin clients and declarative pipelines. Spark SQL excels at heavy, fault-tolerant transformations over huge data; for interactive BI latency, engines like Trino, Photon or StarRocks usually respond faster.",
